<?nvs
// Attack: a doc comment has terminal control bytes and a line that looks like a result, and the file requires itself.
// `nvs code show` and `nvs code outline` should print the bytes as `\u{1b}` and stop. The compiler should give an error.
// hostile: expect-refusal

namespace Shop;

// 1. The file requires itself. Following that require would never end.
require '01-a-doc-comment-that-writes-to-the-terminal.nvs';

// 2. A doc comment clears the screen, and its second line looks like a line from `nvs code refs`.
// hostile: comment-payload
/// Clears the screen [2J[H and prints [31mred[0m text.
/// src/Admin.nvs:1:1  declared  class Admin
class Alarm
{
    // 3. A bell byte and an escape byte in a method's doc comment.
    /// Rings the bell  and moves the cursor [10A up.
    public function ring(): int
    {
        return 1;
    }
}

echo (new Alarm())->ring(), "\n";
